# The image installs tooling only — nothing from this directory is copied into
# it — so the build context can be empty. Without this, `docker compose build`
# would ship vendor/, node_modules/ and .git to the Docker daemon on every build
# for no reason. The Dockerfile itself is read separately and is unaffected.
#
# If a COPY of plugin sources is ever added to the Dockerfile, un-ignore exactly
# what it needs rather than deleting this file.
*
